### API Aggregator — sample requests (VS Code REST Client / Visual Studio / Rider)

@api = http://localhost:5247
@keycloak = http://localhost:8080

### Health (always anonymous)
GET {{api}}/health

### --- Auth: get a JWT via Keycloak password grant (user demo/demo) ---
# @name token
POST {{keycloak}}/realms/aggregator/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=aggregator-api&username=demo&password=demo

### Capture the access token from the response above
@bearer = {{token.response.body.access_token}}

### Aggregated feed — defaults (all sources)
GET {{api}}/api/feed
Authorization: Bearer {{bearer}}

### Feed — weather for a city + search term, small page
GET {{api}}/api/feed?city=Berlin&searchTerm=dotnet&pageSize=5&maxItemsPerSource=5
Authorization: Bearer {{bearer}}

### Feed — only news, newest first
GET {{api}}/api/feed?category=news&sortBy=Timestamp&order=Descending
Authorization: Bearer {{bearer}}

### Feed — most-starred repositories about kubernetes
GET {{api}}/api/feed?searchTerm=kubernetes&category=repository&sortBy=Relevance&order=Descending&pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{bearer}}

### Feed — filter by source and date range
GET {{api}}/api/feed?source=spaceflight-news&from=2026-01-01T00:00:00Z
Authorization: Bearer {{bearer}}

### Request statistics
GET {{api}}/api/statistics
Authorization: Bearer {{bearer}}

### --- Validation error example (pageSize out of range -> 400) ---
GET {{api}}/api/feed?pageSize=0
Authorization: Bearer {{bearer}}

### --- Running with Authentication:Enabled=false? Drop the Authorization headers. ---
